L000771	\subsection{Anyon types, fusion rules, and braiding}\label{append-sub:anyon-type}
L000772	
L000773	Given a finite group $G$, the quantum double of $G$ (also known as the $G$ Drinfeld double, denoted as $\mathcal{D}(G)$)~\cite{kitaev2003fault}, has  anyon type specified by $(C,\chi)$, where $C$ is a conjugacy class and $\chi$ is an irreducible representation of the centralizer $Z(r)$ for a representative $r$ in $C$. The 8 possible anyon types in $S_3$ quantum double are given below:
L000774	
L000775	\begin{table}[h]
L000776	\centering
L000777	\setlength{\tabcolsep}{6pt}
L000778	\begin{tabular}{c c c c c}
L000779	\toprule
L000780	\textbf{Conjugacy class} & \textbf{Centralizer} & \textbf{Charge} & \(d\)\\
L000781	\midrule
L000782	\multirow{3}{*}{\(C_{1}\)} &
L000783	\multirow{3}{*}{\(Z(e)=S_{3}\)} &
L000784	\([+]\) & 1\\
L000785	& & \([-]\) & 1\\
L000786	& & \([2]\) & 2\\
L000787	\midrule
L000788	\multirow{2}{*}{\(C_{2}\)} &
L000789	\multirow{2}{*}{\(Z(\sigma)\cong \mathbb{Z}_{2}\)} &
L000790	\([+]\) & 3\\
L000791	& & \([-]\) & 3\\
L000792	\midrule
L000793	\multirow{3}{*}{\(C_{3}\)} &
L000794	\multirow{3}{*}{\(Z(\mu)\cong \mathbb{Z}_{3}\)} &
L000795	\([1]\) & 2\\
