L000999	The $[2]$ charge ribbon operator circuit above illustrate how a unitary ribbon operator can be decomposed into three steps (as divided by dotted line): 1) ungauging, 2) finite-depth local unitary (FDLU) circuit in a simpler TO, and 3) regauging~\cite{lyons-2025}. For the ungauging step, it is a sequential unitary circuit that "unzip" the direct edges to a simpler TO (in this case ungauging to $\mathbb{Z}_3$ toric code). Then, the FDLU circuit is just the usual string operator for the $e$ anyons in $\mathbb{Z}_3$ toric code. Finally, the regauging layer is used to "zip up" the direct edges back to $S_3$ TO.
